Modifications (October 2026):
- Ported the osu! stable memory reader from TypeScript and C++ to Rust.
- Kept only the selected beatmap, the songs folder and the beatmap file paths;
  removed the HTTP/WebSocket server, overlays, PP calculation, osu!lazer
  support and all other game state readers.
- Exposed the result as a Rust library crate with its own public API.
- Added translation of Windows paths through Wine drive mappings on Linux.

Origin of each file:
  src/stable.rs           packages/tosu/src/memory/stable.ts
  src/paths.rs            packages/tosu/src/instances/osuInstance.ts,
                          packages/tosu/src/states/beatmap.ts
  src/beatmap.rs          packages/common/enums/osu.ts
  src/pattern.rs          packages/tsprocess/lib/memory/memory.h,
                          packages/tsprocess/src/process.ts
  src/process/mod.rs      packages/tsprocess/lib/memory/memory.h,
                          packages/tsprocess/lib/functions.cc,
                          packages/tsprocess/src/process.ts
  src/process/linux.rs    packages/tsprocess/lib/memory/memory_linux.cc,
                          packages/tsprocess/src/process.ts
  src/process/windows.rs  packages/tsprocess/lib/memory/memory_windows.cc
  src/lib.rs, src/error.rs, src/difficulty.rs, examples/watch.rs:
